#{[17592186396751 #edb/ref 1080 "evaluating at $t=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396751 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396751 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b5d015d-eaf2-5953-a208-79b9f37e4968" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396752 #edb/ref 1080 "applying a change of variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396752 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396752 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "30eef7f5-8b22-5be9-9b66-818bc874eb41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396753 #edb/ref 1080 "substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396753 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396753 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1f580aa1-90f1-5a47-b37e-9bf7b327dcaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396754 #edb/ref 1080 "differentiating and using the product rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396754 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396754 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5548b470-04df-52fd-9078-8aee9471580b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186396766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the inhomogeneous system  ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. A derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${y}^{′}(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t)$  \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $y(t)-y({t}_{0})={\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $y({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0})$ \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $y(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t)=x(t)$\n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by  \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by  \n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by  \n{{field-3}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8e9e9aa1-972a-5335-8521-470987b0b354" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396755 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Starting from\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nin $\\text{L2}$ and substituting ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t)$ from the original system gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{substituting }{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ Evaluating $y(t)={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)$ at $t={t}_{0}$ gives\n\n$$\ny({t}_{0})={e}^{-A({t}_{0}-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})=Ix({t}_{0})=x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by $\\text{evaluating at }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ Multiplying both sides of\n\n$$\ny(t)=x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,ds\n$$\n\nfrom $\\text{L6}$ by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L7}$ follows from $\\text{L6}$ by $\\text{multiplying both sides by }{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186396760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186396760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396756 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "af7ae7ba-6ace-5d3b-a3df-d31722ff9859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396757 #edb/ref 1080 "differentiating and using the sum rule" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396757 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396757 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6340a434-1f61-5e6a-a285-4fc8d1b9102a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396758 #edb/ref 1080 "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t+{t}_{0})}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396758 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396758 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8b331929-7f99-5db3-bfa8-928f56ab52cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396759 #edb/ref 1080 "multiplying both sides by ${e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396759 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396759 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a9383354-b3ca-54ba-be42-38ef63dbcfa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396760 #edb/ref 1080 "evaluating at $t={t}_{0}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186396760 #edb/ref 1082 #edb